{
  "kind": "pose",
  "note": "Browsing on the spot, held: the head stays down through a run of chews, tugs a mouthful free, settles and chews on. Starts and ends at the same browse hold `eat-down` leaves the animal in and `eat-up` takes it out of, so a world can play it any whole number of times to feed for as long as it likes. The chew is mostly YAW, not pitch -- a ruminant grinds side to side, and a pure up-down bob reads as a bird pecking, which also makes the chew invisible in a side contact sheet. All four feet stay at their rest positions throughout, so the animal is standing still and eating rather than shuffling. The beat of stillness before the loop point is deliberate: it hides the seam, and a browsing animal does pause.",
